WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.040
Tonight on "secrets declassified."

2
00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:12.080
the close calls that nearly
triggered armageddon

3
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:16.280
and the doomsday plans
designed to survive it.

4
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.600
From the Soviet secret nuclear train...

5
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:21.040
It looks like a normal railway car.

6
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:24.360
but on the inside is armageddon on rails.

7
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.520
To NATO war games that
pushed the kremlin to red alert.

8
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:32.400
The Soviets could have nukes
in the air within 30 minutes.

9
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.320
Or a Soviet submariner standing alone

10
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:37.880
to prevent nuclear apocalypse.

11
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.840
If he just follows orders.
the planet is done.

12
00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.720
These are the astonishing
and sometimes terrible things

13
00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:48.040
done by governments and
the people who work for them.

14
00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:50.600
It's time to bring them to light.

15
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:58.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

16
00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:02.080
A moving target is harder to hit.

17
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:03.840
So when the kremlin wants to shield

18
00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:07.280
its nuclear launch sites
from a U.S. first strike.

19
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.680
it doesn't just camouflage them.

20
00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:12.120
It puts them on wheels.

21
00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:19.720
It's late 1983. and the
kremlin is panicking.

22
00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:21.400
The U.S. has just deployed

23
00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:23.840
new pershing ii missiles
in west Germany.

24
00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.880
And the Soviets believe
these missiles can hit

25
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.240
Moscow in under 10 minutes.

26
00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:32.360
The communists are
concerned that a surprise attack

27
00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.840
could take out all of their nuclear silos

28
00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.680
before they have an
opportunity to counterattack.

29
00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:41.680
So the Soviets need a
new mobile missile system

30
00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:43.520
that they can hide from the U.S.

31
00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:45.400
And launch from anywhere.

32
00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:48.120
Soviet war planners find a solution

33
00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:53.240
the Soviet rail system.

34
00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:55.440
The Soviet union is enormous.

35
00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:57.920
It runs across 11 time zones

36
00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:00.960
and has 100.000 miles
of railway running over it.

37
00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:03.480
This huge rail network is bigger

38
00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.360
than the U.S.'s entire
interstate highway system.

39
00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.480
The thinking is that. if
they put an icbm on a train.

40
00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.680
they can run it across all of this track.

41
00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:15.360
across 11 time zones. leaving
the Americans never knowing

42
00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.160
just where it might actually be.

43
00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.560
The kremlin hands the top-secret project

44
00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:23.720
to a proven rocket
scientist. Vladimir utkin.

45
00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:25.600
Utkin is something of a genius.

46
00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:28.360
He's one of the best rocket
scientists in the Soviet union.

47
00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:30.160
His team has already built the Soviet's

48
00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:35.280
most powerful icbm. a
monster nicknamed Satan.

49
00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.200
Even utkin is a little daunted
by the task before him.

50
00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:40.720
He calls it "amazing in its grandeur."

51
00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:44.520
which I'm pretty sure is
Russian for "this is insane."

52
00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.480
Utkin now has to design a missile that

53
00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:50.880
can be safely launched
not from a concrete silo

54
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.160
but from a train.

55
00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:55.320
At the time. the Soviet union is using

56
00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:58.080
what's called a hot
launch for icbm rockets.

57
00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.520
Basically. this means
that the engine ignites.

58
00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:03.200
and as it does. out
come the exhaust fumes.

59
00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.440
and that's what's firing
the rocket off into the air.

60
00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:07.880
These fumes coming
out of the rocket can reach

61
00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:11.080
temperatures similar to
that at the surface of the sun.

62
00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.600
around 10.000 degrees fahrenheit.

63
00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:15.280
So what you're going to end up with

64
00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:18.360
is tracks and railroad cars
that have been reduced

65
00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:20.680
to puddles of liquid metal.

66
00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.320
So utkin developed something

67
00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:24.840
called a cold launch. and
this uses compressed gas

68
00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:26.360
to launch the rocket instead.

69
00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:28.960
Basically. think of it like popping the cork

70
00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:30.080
on a champagne bottle.

71
00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:34.680
Once it's safely in the air
and away from the railroad car.

72
00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:38.680
it fires up its conventional
engines. and off it goes.

73
00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:41.880
It's a win for utkin.

74
00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.920
but now he faces another challenge.

75
00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:47.760
Normal icbms are just too big to fit

76
00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:50.000
in a Soviet train carriage.

77
00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:52.280
To stay hidden. utkin needs to fit

78
00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:55.680
his new missile system inside
a standard sized freight car.

79
00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.160
That's a problem.

80
00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:59.320
Freight cars are about 80 feet long.

81
00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:02.920
and Satan is 120 feet long.

82
00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:05.160
The math just doesn't work.

83
00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:08.000
Utkin's solution is ingenious.

84
00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.720
Now. utkin can't shrink the rocket.

85
00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:12.720
nor can he expand the freight car.

86
00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:15.000
However. he could do
something with the nose.

87
00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:18.360
So he decides to make
the nose collapsible.

88
00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.640
He creates a kind of origami design

89
00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:24.200
made of corrugated metal.
which folds down inside the rocket

90
00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:26.080
like an accordion.

91
00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.480
Once it's launched.

92
00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:30.120
compressed gases
reinflate the nose cone.

93
00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:33.480
returning it to its perfect
aerodynamic shape.

94
00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:37.760
Utkin calls his new missle the molodets.

95
00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:39.760
Russian for "good job."

96
00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:42.520
Now he just needs a train to put it on.

97
00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:44.480
So the Soviets create what is known

98
00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:47.200
as the combat railway missile system.

99
00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:49.920
It looks completely
ordinary on the outside.

100
00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:52.400
but it's got a missile on the inside.

101
00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:55.480
This is armageddon on wheels.

102
00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:57.520
When it's time for the missiles to launch.

103
00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:00.480
the first thing that happens
is hydraulic legs extend

104
00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.560
out of the train and
touch down on the ground

105
00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:04.920
in order to stabilize the train car.

106
00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:07.280
An arm comes out of the top

107
00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:10.000
to move any power lines out of the way.

108
00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:14.120
The roof splits open. and the
molodets missile goes vertical

109
00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:17.000
and is ready to launch.

110
00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:20.560
Starting in 1987. the Soviets built 12

111
00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:23.280
top secret nuclear ghost trains.

112
00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:26.080
which patrolled the railways for years.

113
00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:30.560
completely unknown to
the public. but not to the CIA.

114
00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:34.480
Only in 1999. the CIA
declassifies its files

115
00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.440
on the apocalypse express.

116
00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.720
The files show that the CIA
did know about these trains

117
00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.760
from their spies back in the 1980s.

118
00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:49.160
The files also revealed
that the Soviet camouflage

119
00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:52.280
was startlingly effective.

120
00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:54.640
The U.S. knew that the trains existed.

121
00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:57.400
But frustratingly. they couldn't find them.

122
00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:01.240
So even if the U.S.
struck all of their fixed silos.

123
00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:03.120
the Soviets would still be able to launch

124
00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:05.480
a devastating retaliatory strike

125
00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:07.680
from their hidden nuclear trains.

126
00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.800
The system worked perfectly.

127
00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:15.440
From doomsday trains
to doomsday planes.

128
00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:17.640
when nuclear missiles start flying.

129
00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:19.880
most governments head underground.

130
00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.760
But not the U.S. president.

131
00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:23.760
He heads to a command center built

132
00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:25.800
to survive armageddon.

133
00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:30.040
one that hides 30.000 feet up in the air.

134
00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:37.120
In the aftermath of the
attacks of September 11th.

135
00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:38.760
there is absolute panic.

136
00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:41.160
and a bigger question starts to form.

137
00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:43.720
Will other attacks be coming?

138
00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:46.440
Just minutes after the
assault on the Pentagon.

139
00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:48.680
observers in the capital are terrified

140
00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:51.520
by another potential threat in the sky.

141
00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:54.240
People spot this mysterious aircraft

142
00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:56.440
circling above Washington D.C..

143
00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:58.840
like it's watching over
the city in lockdown.

144
00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:01.160
The aircraft looks like a jumbo jet

145
00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:03.160
with one key difference.

146
00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:05.280
If you look at the plane
and you compare it

147
00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:07.720
to a traditional 747.

148
00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:10.240
there's a big hump on
the back of the plane.

149
00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:12.160
Confusion turns to fear.

150
00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:15.520
News agencies scramble
to find out if this aircraft

151
00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:18.560
is friend or foe.

152
00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:23.760
To calm the public.
Pentagon sources come clean.

153
00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:25.560
The plane is one of theirs.

154
00:07:27.640 --> 00:07:31.600
It's president George
w. Bush's wartime ride.

155
00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:37.960
the e-4b. known to insiders
as the doomsday plane.

156
00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:44.840
This is essentially a nuclear
command and control in the air.

157
00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:49.640
Now president bush's secret
apocalypse escape machine

158
00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:51.480
has been exposed to the world.

159
00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:53.440
With president bush in Florida.

160
00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:56.000
its 9/11 mission is a mystery.

161
00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:58.040
People wonder if the government knew

162
00:07:58.160 --> 00:07:59.840
something was going to happen

163
00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:01.920
and launched the
doomsday plane in advance.

164
00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:05.040
But in reality. it just so
happens that the doomsday plane

165
00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:07.640
is actually engaged in a standard drill

166
00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:10.760
while the attacks are ongoing.

167
00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:12.760
Now the press and public want to know

168
00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:14.400
more about the plane.

169
00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:18.400
Is the strange hump
concealing a weapon system?

170
00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:22.240
The government decides to open up.

171
00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:24.560
The administration gives
journalists permission

172
00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:28.600
to film inside so the public
can see the inner workings

173
00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:31.240
of the doomsday plane.

174
00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:34.440
The e-4b doomsday
plane's been in service

175
00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:37.320
out of the public eye since 1980.

176
00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:40.200
Now the government
reveals it is a fully functional

177
00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:42.440
Pentagon in the sky.

178
00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:47.760
The doomsday plane can
support up to 112 personnel.

179
00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:50.760
You've got a command
center. a conference room.

180
00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:53.560
even a briefing room where
the president can address

181
00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:55.760
whatever's left of the nation.

182
00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:58.320
Further back. you've
got the operations area.

183
00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:01.360
where 30 specialists
sit glued to their screens.

184
00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:06.080
monitoring intel and the status
of every U.S. asset worldwide.

185
00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:07.880
One way to think of this thing

186
00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:12.600
is like an underground
bunker with wings.

187
00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:15.240
The Pentagon also reveals what's inside

188
00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:17.120
the mysterious hump.

189
00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:19.400
It's the plane's vital heart.

190
00:09:19.520 --> 00:09:23.000
allowing the president to
command a nuclear war

191
00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:25.320
from the skies.

192
00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:28.240
Inside that hump is
the most sophisticated

193
00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:31.320
communication suite that's
ever been put into the air.

194
00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:35.200
It has 67 satellite dishes to ensure that.

195
00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:38.040
even if one form of communication fails.

196
00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:40.080
there are lots of backups.

197
00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:43.520
The hump allows the president
to speak to anybody. anywhere

198
00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:45.400
across the surface of the world.

199
00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:48.200
as long as they can answer a phone.

200
00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:50.440
If world war III breaks out.

201
00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:54.080
the most important people
for the president to contact

202
00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:56.360
may not be on the surface

203
00:09:56.480 --> 00:10:01.360
but lurking deep down at
the bottom of the ocean.

204
00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:04.120
Coiled up in the belly
of the doomsday plane

205
00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:06.920
is a 5-mile-long wire antenna.

206
00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.960
And in a worst-case scenario.

207
00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:11.760
it can be unspooled behind the aircraft.

208
00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:15.320
The wire transmits very
low frequency radio signals.

209
00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:17.520
These radio signals are the only ones

210
00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:20.560
capable of penetrating
beneath the surface of the water

211
00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:24.400
to communicate with U.S.
nuclear armed submarines.

212
00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:27.120
This simple wire lets the president

213
00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:29.240
give the subs that final

214
00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:32.800
apocalyptic order to
retaliate and unleash hell.

215
00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:38.880
So even if the nation is a graveyard.

216
00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:42.240
its capacity for vengeance
is very much alive.

217
00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:48.320
The tragedy of 9/11
exposed the president's

218
00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:52.680
top secret e-4b doomsday
plane to the public.

219
00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:54.520
It's still on duty

220
00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:57.440
but in a world of heightened tensions.

221
00:10:57.560 --> 00:11:02.440
In 2024. the air force
awards a $13 billion contract

222
00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:05.920
to create an upgraded replacement.

223
00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:08.040
The details of those improvements

224
00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:11.720
remain a tightly guarded secret.

225
00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:14.880
Coming up. the Pentagon builds

226
00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:18.480
a wonder weapon so
dangerous. they don't dare test it.

227
00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:21.440
This monster is an apocalypse machine

228
00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:24.720
powered by an
unshielded nuclear reactor.

229
00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:28.680
And later. on the most
dangerous day in history.

230
00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:33.800
a lone Soviet submariner must
decide the fate of the planet.

231
00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:37.360
If he gives the word. he
could start world war III.

232
00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:49.200
Nuclear weapons are designed
to instill fear into the enemy.

233
00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:52.960
But in the 1950s. the U.S.
builds an apocalypse machine

234
00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:56.040
of such awesome
power. even its makers are

235
00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:58.000
terrified to test it.

236
00:11:58.120 --> 00:12:01.120
They call it the flying crowbar.

237
00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:08.520
By 1957. in Washington.
there's a new paranoia.

238
00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:10.000
The Soviets have just introduced

239
00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:11.680
the world's first icbm.

240
00:12:11.800 --> 00:12:13.360
or intercontinental ballistic missile.

241
00:12:13.480 --> 00:12:16.600
So now the Soviets are
capable of striking us first

242
00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:18.360
before we can retaliate.

243
00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:21.080
The Pentagon decides
they need a wonder weapon.

244
00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:24.200
They want something so
terrifyingly overwhelming

245
00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:28.600
that Moscow won't even
dare start a war with the U.S.

246
00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:31.600
They turn to the home of the h-bomb.

247
00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:34.360
Lawrence liver more labs in California.

248
00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:36.760
At liver more. they hand the responsibility

249
00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:38.880
for creating this monster machine

250
00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:42.800
to 37-year-old associate
director Ted merkle.

251
00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:45.360
Merkle assembles a dream team.

252
00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:48.520
the sharpest engineers and
nuclear scientists he can find.

253
00:12:48.640 --> 00:12:52.560
Their job is to invent the most
devastating weapon possible.

254
00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:54.160
The stakes are so high.

255
00:12:54.280 --> 00:12:58.480
he's given a budget
of $230 million a year

256
00:12:58.600 --> 00:13:02.360
in today's money to
bring this vision to life.

257
00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:05.360
The result should be so hellishly deadly

258
00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:08.200
that the mission is
codenamed after the Roman god

259
00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:13.320
of the underworld. project pluto.

260
00:13:13.440 --> 00:13:16.000
Merkle envisions a
missile-bomber hybrid

261
00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:20.160
with no human crew. like a
gigantic nuclear-armed drone.

262
00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:23.760
He wants it to be able to
lurk for days at high altitude.

263
00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:27.800
And he wants to pack
not 1. but 16 nukes.

264
00:13:27.920 --> 00:13:31.040
Soon merkle settles on
a design for the weapon

265
00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:36.240
based on a stainless steel
shell nearly 100 feet long.

266
00:13:36.360 --> 00:13:39.800
It's brutally simple.
designed for destruction.

267
00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:44.160
so merkle calls it the flying crowbar.

268
00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:47.160
First. the crowbar needs
a game-changing engine

269
00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:49.280
to make it airborne.

270
00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:51.520
To keep it in the air for days.

271
00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:53.600
carrying 50.000 pounds of bombs.

272
00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:56.120
merkle comes up with
a solution straight out

273
00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:58.320
of atomic-age science fiction.

274
00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:02.760
He's going to power the
crowbar using a nuclear reactor.

275
00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:05.080
Typically. a nuclear reactor has

276
00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:07.240
a lot of shielding so that people are

277
00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:09.880
protected from the
radiation that it produces.

278
00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:12.960
But all that shielding is just
too darn heavy for a missile.

279
00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:15.600
And given that this aircraft is unmanned.

280
00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:17.840
merkle decides to just ditch the shielding

281
00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:20.160
and save all that weight.

282
00:14:20.280 --> 00:14:24.200
So now you have an
unshielded nuclear reactor.

283
00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:27.160
By the early 1960s. merkle's team has

284
00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:29.680
a full-scale engine prototype ready.

285
00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:31.600
Now they need to test it.

286
00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:34.720
You can't just fire up

287
00:14:34.840 --> 00:14:36.800
an unshielded nuclear reactor anywhere.

288
00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:38.320
You need a place where you can make

289
00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:41.040
a big. giant nuclear wasteland.

290
00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:44.200
So they find a location of 8 square miles

291
00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:47.960
in jackass flats. Nevada.

292
00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:49.640
Once the reactor starts.

293
00:14:49.760 --> 00:14:51.760
the radiation will make it deadly.

294
00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:55.520
Merkle's team builds a
thick-walled concrete bunker

295
00:14:55.640 --> 00:14:57.840
for the reactor to be tested inside of

296
00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:00.040
and a second concrete bunker

297
00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:02.880
for his team to observe the tests.

298
00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:05.160
To solve the problem of
how to move the reactor

299
00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:06.560
once it's running hot.

300
00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:08.480
they build a two-mile railroad track

301
00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:11.640
and its very own
remote-controlled rail car

302
00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:14.240
to move it into position.

303
00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:17.920
On may 22. 1964. the flying crowbar's

304
00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:20.840
full-sized nuclear reactor engine rolls out

305
00:15:20.960 --> 00:15:23.080
for its make-or-break test.

306
00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:26.680
The engine is a monster... 9 feet long.

307
00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:31.400
5 feet in diameter.
weighing 10.000 pounds.

308
00:15:31.520 --> 00:15:35.320
When the test starts.
the roar is deafening.

309
00:15:35.440 --> 00:15:38.360
The reactor glows as
it hits 2.500 degrees.

310
00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:41.360
That's so hot that it melts lead bricks

311
00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:42.560
placed under the tracks.

312
00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:46.840
The test lasts for just five minutes.

313
00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:52.680
Project pluto's nuclear-powered
engine is a success.

314
00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:54.440
Once it's been deployed.

315
00:15:54.560 --> 00:15:56.360
it will drive the crowbar at mach 3

316
00:15:56.480 --> 00:15:59.560
on an apocalyptic multi-stage attack run.

317
00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:01.600
So there are four big threats associated

318
00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:03.520
with the flying crowbar.

319
00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:05.560
Number one is the
shock wave it produces.

320
00:16:05.680 --> 00:16:08.600
Because the weapon
is traveling at mach 3.

321
00:16:08.720 --> 00:16:13.400
it's producing a shock wave
that can flatten buildings.

322
00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:15.280
Number two is the
unshielded nuclear reactor

323
00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:16.760
that's powering it.

324
00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:18.560
When it's flying. it's. of course. leaving

325
00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:21.800
a path of radioactivity as it flies.

326
00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:25.560
It's carrying a payload
of 16 nuclear weapons.

327
00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:28.160
It can drop them one at a time.

328
00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:31.200
each with the power to destroy a city.

329
00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:34.240
And lastly. the crowbar itself is a bomb.

330
00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:38.000
So it can be programmed
to target one final bullseye

331
00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:39.440
and take it out.

332
00:16:41.360 --> 00:16:44.920
It will be horrifyingly efficient.

333
00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:48.000
The nuclear reactor
engine works on the ground.

334
00:16:48.120 --> 00:16:50.560
Now the pluto team needs to flight test

335
00:16:50.680 --> 00:16:54.760
the flying crowbar in real-world skies.

336
00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:58.680
Where on earth can you flight
test a weapon that devastating?

337
00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:01.400
The Nevada test range is
way too close to Las Vegas.

338
00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:04.720
and even the pacific
test areas are too risky.

339
00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:06.680
While the pluto team are grappling

