00:25:41.680 --> 00:25:44.720
"nuclear innocents."

512
00:25:44.840 --> 00:25:46.080
Then they briefed them on their

513
00:25:46.160 --> 00:25:48.680
top secret science assignment.

514
00:25:48.800 --> 00:25:52.480
building an atom bomb from scratch.

515
00:25:52.600 --> 00:25:54.080
Dobson's first thought?

516
00:25:54.200 --> 00:25:57.160
Sounds like a bit of a challenge.

517
00:25:58.920 --> 00:26:00.480
This working group is tucked into

518
00:26:00.600 --> 00:26:02.320
a small office at liver more.

519
00:26:02.440 --> 00:26:04.040
Although they have security clearance.

520
00:26:04.160 --> 00:26:07.080
they don't have access to
any classified information.

521
00:26:07.200 --> 00:26:09.320
And as this is the analog era.

522
00:26:09.440 --> 00:26:11.560
that means that they
can go to the public library.

523
00:26:11.680 --> 00:26:13.520
and they can go to the university library.

524
00:26:13.640 --> 00:26:17.040
All they have access to
are published sources.

525
00:26:17.160 --> 00:26:19.640
But everything that this
working group produces

526
00:26:19.760 --> 00:26:21.600
immediately becomes top secret.

527
00:26:21.720 --> 00:26:24.200
First. the young scientists must decide

528
00:26:24.320 --> 00:26:27.120
what kind of atomic bomb to make.

529
00:26:27.240 --> 00:26:28.880
They've got two choices.

530
00:26:29.000 --> 00:26:31.480
They could attempt to build
either a uranium-based bomb

531
00:26:31.600 --> 00:26:33.600
or a plutonium-based bomb.

532
00:26:33.720 --> 00:26:35.360
Uranium is a simpler bomb.

533
00:26:35.480 --> 00:26:37.760
You can just shove one mass of uranium

534
00:26:37.880 --> 00:26:40.280
into another to create an explosion.

535
00:26:40.400 --> 00:26:43.280
Plutonium is more powerful but harder

536
00:26:43.400 --> 00:26:46.840
because it requires this very precise

537
00:26:46.960 --> 00:26:50.400
three-stage explosion to make it work.

538
00:26:50.520 --> 00:26:52.480
They want to impress
the scientists at liver more.

539
00:26:52.560 --> 00:26:54.760
so they go with plutonium.

540
00:26:54.880 --> 00:26:57.040
Next they hit the library.

541
00:26:57.160 --> 00:26:58.680
As they seek a way forward.

542
00:26:58.800 --> 00:27:00.840
they're looking for whatever information

543
00:27:00.960 --> 00:27:02.880
they can find in the public domain.

544
00:27:03.000 --> 00:27:06.280
And they get lucky because
they find this unclassified report

545
00:27:06.400 --> 00:27:08.200
from the Manhattan project.

546
00:27:08.320 --> 00:27:10.840
So it's kind of like a road map.

547
00:27:10.960 --> 00:27:13.240
But the report is so heavily redacted.

548
00:27:13.360 --> 00:27:15.400
it's of little use in the end.

549
00:27:15.520 --> 00:27:16.976
Once they've gone
through the document.

550
00:27:17.000 --> 00:27:18.720
it's all just nothing but disappointment.

551
00:27:20.360 --> 00:27:22.280
For months they struggle.

552
00:27:22.400 --> 00:27:24.176
even feeling paranoid
and wondering if they're

553
00:27:24.200 --> 00:27:25.200
being set up to fail.

554
00:27:25.320 --> 00:27:27.360
But still. they keep going.

555
00:27:27.480 --> 00:27:29.800
These are smart and resourceful men.

556
00:27:29.920 --> 00:27:31.456
and they understand that
they don't know anything

557
00:27:31.480 --> 00:27:33.160
about explosives. and so they begin

558
00:27:33.280 --> 00:27:35.920
a process of educating
themselves on the subject.

559
00:27:36.040 --> 00:27:37.800
Ironically. they get their biggest boost

560
00:27:37.920 --> 00:27:41.000
from eisenhower's 1950s
atoms for peace program.

561
00:27:41.120 --> 00:27:43.760
which declassified nuclear
data for civilian purposes.

562
00:27:43.880 --> 00:27:47.480
So they repurposed
that data for their weapon.

563
00:27:47.600 --> 00:27:50.360
Soon they begin to build their bomb.

564
00:27:50.480 --> 00:27:54.360
But their experiments aren't
even allowed to leave paper.

565
00:27:54.480 --> 00:27:56.960
When these physicists
want to run an experiment.

566
00:27:57.080 --> 00:27:59.760
they have to write out a very
detailed report of exactly what

567
00:27:59.880 --> 00:28:02.560
they want to know and then
give it to their liver more handlers.

568
00:28:02.680 --> 00:28:05.000
They're never told whether
or not the experiments

569
00:28:05.120 --> 00:28:06.520
are actually carried out.

570
00:28:06.640 --> 00:28:09.760
They just get a report
back with the results.

571
00:28:09.880 --> 00:28:13.320
By 1966. after less than three years.

572
00:28:13.440 --> 00:28:16.000
dobson and selden are done.

573
00:28:16.120 --> 00:28:18.480
They have completed
their plan for the device.

574
00:28:18.600 --> 00:28:20.360
It's too big to fit in a missile.

575
00:28:20.480 --> 00:28:23.280
but it is small enough to fit
in the back of a pickup truck.

576
00:28:23.400 --> 00:28:27.200
And the plans are so
detailed that they even boast

577
00:28:27.320 --> 00:28:29.880
that it could be completed
and manufactured

578
00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:31.280
in a machine shop.

579
00:28:33.280 --> 00:28:35.960
Now the question is. will it work?

580
00:28:36.080 --> 00:28:37.800
Have they passed the test?

581
00:28:37.920 --> 00:28:40.080
No one at liver more will tell them.

582
00:28:40.200 --> 00:28:42.160
Dobson and selden
get sent out on the road

583
00:28:42.280 --> 00:28:44.400
on a classified lecture tour.

584
00:28:44.520 --> 00:28:46.880
Government-approved
scientists and military officers

585
00:28:47.000 --> 00:28:48.880
get a chance to question the men about

586
00:28:49.000 --> 00:28:50.760
their assumptions and methods.

587
00:28:50.880 --> 00:28:53.160
After their final q&a.
their liver more handler

588
00:28:53.280 --> 00:28:54.840
pulls them to the side

589
00:28:54.960 --> 00:28:56.840
and lets them in on a little secret.

590
00:28:56.960 --> 00:29:00.360
He tells them that. if
their design is constructed.

591
00:29:00.480 --> 00:29:03.120
it would make a pretty
impressive explosion.

592
00:29:03.240 --> 00:29:06.000
Dobson and selden
want to know how big.

593
00:29:06.120 --> 00:29:09.400
and the answer leaves them stunned.

594
00:29:09.520 --> 00:29:11.280
It would be an explosion comparable

595
00:29:11.400 --> 00:29:15.840
to the Hiroshima bomb.
a 15-kiloton nominal yield.

596
00:29:15.960 --> 00:29:19.440
They've created a diy apocalypse.

597
00:29:19.560 --> 00:29:22.160
It is a spine-chilling result.

598
00:29:22.280 --> 00:29:24.480
In less than three years.

599
00:29:24.600 --> 00:29:27.240
the young physicists
have unlocked the secrets

600
00:29:27.360 --> 00:29:29.120
of mass destruction.

601
00:29:29.240 --> 00:29:32.080
Dobson and selden's
success has the government

602
00:29:32.200 --> 00:29:34.320
really concerned with
nuclear proliferation.

603
00:29:34.440 --> 00:29:36.160
So they pushed forward

604
00:29:36.280 --> 00:29:38.520
with the nuclear non-proliferation treaty.

605
00:29:38.640 --> 00:29:43.960
which is signed by 59 nations in 1968.

606
00:29:44.080 --> 00:29:46.360
The government keeps
the experiment top secret

607
00:29:46.480 --> 00:29:48.560
for four decades

608
00:29:48.680 --> 00:29:51.800
until reports are declassified in 2003.

609
00:29:54.480 --> 00:29:58.000
Even then. the details
reveal far too much

610
00:29:58.120 --> 00:30:01.000
about how to build a nuclear bomb.

611
00:30:01.120 --> 00:30:02.400
The results of this experiment

612
00:30:02.480 --> 00:30:05.200
are deemed so dangerous.

613
00:30:05.320 --> 00:30:07.320
even when they're eventually declassified

614
00:30:07.440 --> 00:30:10.840
and released to the public.
almost every page is redacted.

615
00:30:14.000 --> 00:30:18.240
Coming up. to hide a
nuclear test from the Soviets.

616
00:30:18.360 --> 00:30:21.880
the U.S. pushes their
technology to the limit.

617
00:30:22.000 --> 00:30:23.520
They're going to try and launch a set

618
00:30:23.640 --> 00:30:26.200
of nuclear rockets off the deck of a ship

619
00:30:26.320 --> 00:30:28.760
in one of the roughest
spots in the ocean.

620
00:30:36.120 --> 00:30:37.920
How do you defend
against a nuclear missile

621
00:30:38.000 --> 00:30:40.600
screaming towards you
at 15.000 miles per hour?

622
00:30:40.720 --> 00:30:43.200
In the 1950s. the Pentagon's solution is

623
00:30:43.320 --> 00:30:45.400
straight out of science fiction...

624
00:30:45.520 --> 00:30:48.440
a gigantic radioactive force field

625
00:30:48.560 --> 00:30:51.000
covering the whole of the United States

626
00:30:51.120 --> 00:30:54.640
created by detonating nukes in space.

627
00:30:59.280 --> 00:31:02.080
By the late 1950s. in the
department of defense.

628
00:31:02.200 --> 00:31:04.440
there is an anxiety that the Soviets can

629
00:31:04.560 --> 00:31:06.240
launch an icbm attack.

630
00:31:06.360 --> 00:31:09.080
The United States is working
on the same technology.

631
00:31:09.200 --> 00:31:10.520
but we're not there yet.

632
00:31:10.640 --> 00:31:13.600
What this begins is an era in our history

633
00:31:13.720 --> 00:31:16.960
during which intelligent
people come up with ideas

634
00:31:17.080 --> 00:31:21.240
of how one might stop an icbm attack.

635
00:31:21.360 --> 00:31:22.840
One of the people that comes forward

636
00:31:22.960 --> 00:31:24.520
is Nicholas christofilos.

637
00:31:24.640 --> 00:31:26.880
He's a former elevator repairman

638
00:31:27.000 --> 00:31:29.720
and self-taught physicist
who's now working

639
00:31:29.840 --> 00:31:33.440
at the university of
California's radiation lab.

640
00:31:33.560 --> 00:31:35.720
Christofilos proposes a plan

641
00:31:35.840 --> 00:31:37.800
straight out of science fiction...

642
00:31:37.920 --> 00:31:40.960
a plasma shield in space.

643
00:31:41.080 --> 00:31:45.040
His plan is genius but insane.

644
00:31:45.160 --> 00:31:47.800
Step one. explode a nuclear warhead

645
00:31:47.920 --> 00:31:51.960
300 miles above continental america.

646
00:31:52.080 --> 00:31:55.760
This will release a
cloud of nuclear particles.

647
00:31:55.880 --> 00:31:58.040
Step two. let nature run its course.

648
00:31:58.160 --> 00:32:01.600
Christofilos believes that
earth's magnetic field is going

649
00:32:01.720 --> 00:32:04.720
to trap those particles
above the continent.

650
00:32:04.840 --> 00:32:09.520
essentially creating a
nuclear shield above america.

651
00:32:09.640 --> 00:32:12.016
If the Soviets were to launch
a warhead through that shield.

652
00:32:12.040 --> 00:32:14.840
its electronics would be completely fried.

653
00:32:14.960 --> 00:32:19.640
This will destroy any nuclear
weapon aimed at america.

654
00:32:19.760 --> 00:32:22.000
The two big issues are.
number one. whether or not

655
00:32:22.120 --> 00:32:24.720
the earth's magnetic
field will be strong enough

656
00:32:24.840 --> 00:32:28.880
to hold that radiation in place
to create the desired barrier.

657
00:32:29.000 --> 00:32:31.080
And then number two is whether or not

658
00:32:31.200 --> 00:32:33.640
it will be created in such a concentration

659
00:32:33.760 --> 00:32:36.760
that it can interfere with
electrical systems on an icbm.

660
00:32:36.880 --> 00:32:38.720
There's no way to prove this in a lab.

661
00:32:38.840 --> 00:32:40.120
The only way to do it is

662
00:32:40.240 --> 00:32:41.760
to give it a try and see what happens.

663
00:32:43.520 --> 00:32:47.000
President eisenhower
signs off on the plan.

664
00:32:47.120 --> 00:32:50.120
Project argus is born.

665
00:32:50.240 --> 00:32:52.040
But it's on a tight deadline.

666
00:32:52.160 --> 00:32:54.080
The U.S. and Soviets are negotiating

667
00:32:54.200 --> 00:32:56.200
an end to nuclear testing.

668
00:32:56.320 --> 00:32:59.760
set to kick in by the end of the year.

669
00:32:59.880 --> 00:33:02.040
To beat that deadline. argus has to be

670
00:33:02.160 --> 00:33:04.840
completed in just six months.

671
00:33:04.960 --> 00:33:08.120
That's not very much
time. so the race is on.

672
00:33:08.240 --> 00:33:11.400
The next challenge is secrecy.

673
00:33:11.520 --> 00:33:13.480
If the United States were to conduct

674
00:33:13.600 --> 00:33:16.560
any kind of an experiment.
launching a nuclear weapon

675
00:33:16.680 --> 00:33:19.680
into to earth orbit and detonating it.

676
00:33:19.800 --> 00:33:21.720
the Soviet union would
certainly walk away

677
00:33:21.840 --> 00:33:23.560
from the negotiating table.

678
00:33:23.680 --> 00:33:25.200
That means that they can't use

679
00:33:25.320 --> 00:33:26.840
their normal nuclear test sites...

680
00:33:26.960 --> 00:33:28.440
not the one in Nevada.

681
00:33:28.560 --> 00:33:30.920
not the one in the
bikini atoll in the pacific.

682
00:33:31.040 --> 00:33:33.320
They want a location that's so remote.

683
00:33:33.440 --> 00:33:35.120
that Soviet spies would never know

684
00:33:35.240 --> 00:33:36.960
the tests have ever occurred.

685
00:33:37.080 --> 00:33:39.640
They choose a spot in the
south Atlantic. far out to sea.

686
00:33:39.760 --> 00:33:43.520
more than 600 miles
away from the closest land.

687
00:33:43.640 --> 00:33:45.760
This is one of the
most desolate stretches

688
00:33:45.880 --> 00:33:48.080
on the planet.

689
00:33:48.200 --> 00:33:51.920
Now project argus must
attempt an unprecedented feat...

690
00:33:52.040 --> 00:33:56.280
launch nuclear missiles
from a ship at sea.

691
00:33:56.400 --> 00:33:59.440
To beat the deadline.
they'll have to do it in August.

692
00:33:59.560 --> 00:34:02.320
That's right in the middle
of the south Atlantic winter.

693
00:34:02.440 --> 00:34:05.120
We're talking about the roughest seas.

694
00:34:05.240 --> 00:34:06.800
some of the biggest waves.

695
00:34:06.920 --> 00:34:08.920
some of the fastest winds on earth.

696
00:34:09.040 --> 00:34:11.160
and storms coming from out of nowhere.

697
00:34:11.280 --> 00:34:12.920
It is insane.

698
00:34:14.440 --> 00:34:16.000
In the early morning hours

699
00:34:16.120 --> 00:34:19.040
of August 27th. battered
by the wind and waves.

700
00:34:19.160 --> 00:34:22.320
the argus team fires off their first missile.

701
00:34:24.360 --> 00:34:25.960
The conditions are too difficult.

702
00:34:26.080 --> 00:34:29.240
The missile veers off
course and detonates too low.

703
00:34:30.640 --> 00:34:32.480
Days later. they try again.

704
00:34:32.600 --> 00:34:34.120
That one also fails.

705
00:34:34.240 --> 00:34:36.160
They've got one last chance.

706
00:34:38.240 --> 00:34:41.240
Their third and final attempt
comes on September 6th.

707
00:34:41.360 --> 00:34:44.200
They launch the missile
and hope that it works.

708
00:34:44.320 --> 00:34:46.840
The missile soars 300 miles up

709
00:34:46.960 --> 00:34:48.960
and detonates on target.

710
00:34:49.080 --> 00:34:52.280
The crewmen on deck look up.

711
00:34:52.400 --> 00:34:55.760
and they see this
beautiful man-made Aurora

712
00:34:55.880 --> 00:34:58.000
stretching across the sky.

713
00:34:58.120 --> 00:34:59.920
It's from the radiation they just added

714
00:35:00.040 --> 00:35:01.720
to the magnetic field.

715
00:35:01.840 --> 00:35:04.400
A satellite flies right through it.

716
00:35:04.520 --> 00:35:06.720
and it captures critical data

717
00:35:06.840 --> 00:35:09.280
and beams it right back
down to mission control.

718
00:35:09.400 --> 00:35:11.600
ready for analysis.

719
00:35:11.720 --> 00:35:13.160
The good news...

720
00:35:13.280 --> 00:35:15.720
christofilos is definitely on to something.

721
00:35:15.840 --> 00:35:18.640
The explosion does
create a measurable cloud

722
00:35:18.760 --> 00:35:20.480
of radioactive particles in space.

723
00:35:20.600 --> 00:35:23.360
This becomes a new
phenomenon that is known

724
00:35:23.480 --> 00:35:26.320
as the christofilos effect.

725
00:35:26.440 --> 00:35:28.360
There's bad news too.

726
00:35:28.480 --> 00:35:31.560
The christofilos effect is
nowhere near strong enough

727
00:35:31.680 --> 00:35:33.360
to knock out a missile.

728
00:35:33.480 --> 00:35:35.800
Project argus ends
up costing $100 million

729
00:35:35.920 --> 00:35:37.640
in 21st century dollars.

730
00:35:37.760 --> 00:35:41.600
Within a year of the test.
the project is canceled.

731
00:35:41.720 --> 00:35:43.560
Argus doesn't work.

732
00:35:43.680 --> 00:35:46.280
but the Pentagon
manages to keep it a secret.

733
00:35:46.400 --> 00:35:49.040
That's about to change.

734
00:35:49.160 --> 00:35:51.136
"New York times" reporters
get wind of the story.

735
00:35:51.160 --> 00:35:53.000
but the government
convinces them to sit on it

736
00:35:53.120 --> 00:35:54.960
for national security reasons.

737
00:35:55.080 --> 00:35:57.000
Then. when government
scientists start pushing

738
00:35:57.080 --> 00:35:58.600
to release the argus data.

739
00:35:58.720 --> 00:36:00.576
"the New York times"
doesn't want to be scooped.

740
00:36:00.600 --> 00:36:02.240
so it breaks the story.

741
00:36:12.600 --> 00:36:15.280
It turns out that. primarily
because argus failed.

742
00:36:15.400 --> 00:36:18.480
it does not derail the negotiations

743
00:36:18.600 --> 00:36:20.080
toward the limited test ban treaty.

744
00:36:20.200 --> 00:36:22.240
which becomes a reality in 1963.

745
00:36:22.360 --> 00:36:24.680
And from that moment
forward. there will be no more

746
00:36:24.800 --> 00:36:26.520
atmospheric nuclear testing.

747
00:36:26.640 --> 00:36:30.240
And there will also be no
more nuclear blasts in space.

748
00:36:31.840 --> 00:36:36.960
Coming up... When NATO
war games get too realistic.

749
00:36:37.080 --> 00:36:39.240
the Soviets prepare to strike.

750
00:36:39.360 --> 00:36:40.960
Soviet high command starts moving into

751
00:36:41.040 --> 00:36:42.280
their underground bunkers.

752
00:36:42.400 --> 00:36:44.040
Moscow is freaking out.

753
00:36:51.440 --> 00:36:53.960
In 1983. thousands of
NATO troops mobilize

754
00:36:54.080 --> 00:36:55.640
across Europe.

755
00:36:55.760 --> 00:36:59.600
Nuclear weapons are armed
and loaded onto aircraft.

756
00:36:59.720 --> 00:37:02.680
The impossible question
facing the kremlin:

757
00:37:02.800 --> 00:37:05.720
Is this another military exercise

758
00:37:05.840 --> 00:37:09.040
or the opening move of world war III?

759
00:37:11.960 --> 00:37:14.920
In 1983. Ronald Reagan
referred to the Soviet union

760
00:37:15.040 --> 00:37:16.920
as the evil empire.

761
00:37:17.040 --> 00:37:19.080
For the United States
to demonize the Soviets

762
00:37:19.200 --> 00:37:22.160
in that kind of fashion
suggested that Reagan was

763
00:37:22.280 --> 00:37:24.800
taking on the cold war
as kind of a crusade.

764
00:37:24.920 --> 00:37:29.240
Many in the U.S. recognize
this as simple saber rattling.

765
00:37:29.360 --> 00:37:31.800
However. in Moscow.
they are convinced that.

766
00:37:31.920 --> 00:37:35.480
in fact. the United
States is on the warpath.

767
00:37:35.600 --> 00:37:39.800
And it's a powder keg of
paranoia into which NATO is

768
00:37:39.920 --> 00:37:43.000
about to drop a lighted match.

769
00:37:43.120 --> 00:37:46.120
On November 7th. senior officers gather

770
00:37:46.240 --> 00:37:49.960
at NATO hq in Belgium.
ready for the culmination

771
00:37:50.080 --> 00:37:52.440
of their annual war games.

